# Response headers.
#
# These live here rather than in netlify.toml on purpose: Netlify only reads
# netlify.toml for a repository-connected deploy. A drag-and-drop or API/zip
# deploy ignores it entirely, which would silently ship the site with no CSP
# at all. `_headers` is honoured in every deploy mode, so it is the single
# source of truth and netlify.toml keeps only the build config.
#
# Syntax is the same path-matching Netlify uses in netlify.toml.

# The font filenames are stable, NOT content-hashed (fonts/inter.woff2), so a
# long immutable cache would pin a client to a replaced file for a year with no
# way to invalidate it. Thirty days keeps the win and bounds the mistake: to
# ship a new font, rename the file.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

# Security headers.
#   * X-Frame-Options + frame-ancestors 'none' - the portal is never iframed.
#   * script-src 'self' - no inline script anywhere in the page, which is also
#     why the theme bootstrap lives in theme-init.js instead of a <script> tag.
#     This blocks Netlify's injected free-plan badge, which is intended.
#   * connect-src allows *.netlify.app because the reachability check pings the
#     deployed dashboards. If a dashboard ever moves to a custom domain, add
#     that origin here or its pill will read "Could not verify".
#   * frame-src allows *.netlify.app because a row's preview embeds the
#     dashboard itself. Without it the preview would be blocked by OUR policy
#     and look like the dashboard's fault. Same custom-domain caveat as above.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://*.netlify.app; frame-src https://*.netlify.app; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'
